  "configuration_id": "config_037",
  "reason": "The current best (config_009, acc=0.6352) uses pca_n2000 + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted. The only untested dimension for this top-performing combination is aggregation type: all top configs use avgpool, but transformer aggregation has never been paired with this exact set of encoders and weighted fusion. config_037 (pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) isolates that single change. Evidence strongly favors pca_n2000 over scgpt (0.61–0.64 vs 0.51) and imagenet_vit_l over resnet50 (0.63 vs 0.62), so exploring a different aggregation on this proven backbone is the highest-information next step. If transformer aggregation captures cross-profile interactions better than simple averaging, it could push accuracy above 0.635; if not, it confirms avgpool is optimal and the remaining 3 experiments can target other levers. Expected cost: moderate—transformer aggregation adds self-attention over profiles on top of the ViT-L backbone, so I estimate roughly 10–15 GPU hours (about 1.5–2× config_009's 7.02 hrs), which is well within the remaining budget of ~47 GPU hours."
}

